{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791805702,"nonce":"2crmfLa4l4egvDGhXysxWTPEVBk=","message":"Implementation milestone for e8a1b50:\n\nAdded shared Size.Sm/Md/Lg (Md default) to Input, Textarea, Select, Combobox, InputOtp, Checkbox, RadioGroup, Slider and Badge. CSS sizes fonts, padding, shape-token radii and internal parts together. Select option classes carry the density into the top layer; RadioGroupItem inherits group size and accepts an individual override.\n\nEditable text now follows resolved CSS metrics, and textarea wrapping follows the actual inner box. Geometry hooks run on restyle/layout, with owner cleanup; no idle ticker was added. SVG intrinsic dimensions are CSS defaults, explicit attributes retain priority, and removing size rules restores the document's dimensions.\n\nValidation: tests/run.sh exits 0, with 1,054 successful checks, including 149 existing component checks and 73 focused sizing checks covering focus/reveal, OTP editing, label activation, radio keyboard navigation, dropdown rows, horizontal/vertical seeking, disabled controls, overrides and intrinsic SVG restoration.\n\nVisual follow-up: the new FormsGallery SIZES=1 capture exposes a native SF Mono rasterization failure on macOS. A glyph requested at 32 px returns an image roughly 1,020 x 1,503 px, overflows the atlas, and clears the frame's text. Reproduced in interpreter and hybrid. Temporary native diagnostic builds are isolated under /private/tmp, not part of the component implementation. Continuing visual verification and tracking this separately.","files":null}]}